---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import FounderCard from "../components/FounderCard.astro";
import AuditCTA from "../components/AuditCTA.astro";
import { founders } from "../data/founders";
---
<Base
  title="About The Micro Agency"
  description="A specialist Microsoft Advertising agency built to close the skills gap most UK advertisers leave open. Pro-intelligence, not anti-Google."
>
  <PageHeader
    kicker="About"
    title="A specialist, built to close a skills gap"
    intro="Microsoft is a billion-user ecosystem that most UK advertisers run no properly optimised campaigns on. That is not an awareness problem. It is a specialism problem. We exist to fix it."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow prose">
      <p>
        The Micro Agency is pro-intelligence, not anti-Google. Google is where
        most demand is captured and it should stay that way. But concentrating
        almost all of search spend on one engine is a measurable risk, and
        Microsoft's ecosystem holds audiences, targeting and pricing that
        generalists leave on the table because nobody on the team owns it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The name works on two levels. Micro as in Microsoft, the platform we
        specialise in. Micro as in a lean, senior boutique, where the people who
        win the work are the people who do it. We do one thing, and we do it
        properly: build for the Microsoft ecosystem from the ground up, and prove
        the incremental value it adds.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>{founders.length > 1 ? "The founders" : "Founder"}</h2>
      <div
        class:list={[
          "mt-8 grid gap-6",
          founders.length > 1 ? "md:grid-cols-2" : "max-w-xl",
        ]}
      >
        {founders.map((f) => <FounderCard founder={f} />)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <AuditCTA />
</Base>
